        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "149576fe-f613-509a-bede-1a3734336bb2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Bhupen Hazarika\n- Organizations: Sangeet Natak Akademi, Government of India\n- Awards: Padmashri, Sangeet Natak Akademi Award, Dada Saheb Phalke Award, Padmabhushan, Sangeet Natak Akademi Fellowship\n- Concepts: National Academy for Music, Dance and Drama, performing arts\n\nFacts:\n- The Government of India set up Sangeet Natak Akademi as the national-level academy for performing arts in India.\n- Sangeet Natak Akademi is The National Academy for Music, Dance and Drama in English.\n- Bhupen Hazarika received the Padmashri in 1977.\n- Bhupen Hazarika received the Sangeet Natak Akademi Award in 1987.\n- Bhupen Hazarika received the Dada Saheb Phalke Award in 1992, which is India's highest award in cinema, from the Government of India.\n- Bhupen Hazarika received the Padmabhushan in 2001.\n- Bhupen Hazarika received the Sangeet Natak Akademi Fellowship in 2008, which is the highest award of Sangeet Natak Akademi.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d2c65679-6024-5b7d-a0bf-65b13aa37a19",
        "text": "Page: Bhupen Hazarika. Sentence: Recipient of Sangeet Natak Akademi Award (1987), Padmashri (1977), and Padmabhushan (2001), Hazarika was awarded with Dada Saheb Phalke Award (1992), India's highest award in cinema, by the Government of India and Sangeet Natak Akademi Fellowship (2008), the highest award of the Sangeet Natak Akademi, India's The National Academy for Music, Dance and Drama.\nPage: Sangeet Natak Akademi. Sentence: Sangeet Natak Akademi (Devanāgarī: \"संगीत नाटक अकादेमी\" or The National Academy for Music, Dance and Drama in English) is the national level academy for performing arts set up by the Government of India.",
